/P 18 0 R
/E (Our pipeline recovers major scene layout, object placement, and dominant structures across different indoor Replica environments)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [84]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 18 0 R
/E (The perception modules provide useful but imperfect signals: dense monocular depth gives per-frame geometry, while long-term tracks connect the same scene points across frames. Our pipeline brings these together using multi-view reprojection consistency, checking whether tracked points can be explained by one rigid 3D scene. Rather than retraining the models, it refines only geometric variables: camera poses, global scale and per-frame depth corrections. A fast rigidity filter removes inconsistent tracks, while global bundle adjustment refines camera trajectories and depth alignment by minimising reprojection error, producing corrected depth maps and a consistent trajectory for TSDF fusion.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [85]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 18 0 R
/E (On the Replica dataset [4], beyond the reported F@5cm result, our pipeline reaches F@10cm of 80.8% and F@15cm of 88.3%, indicating stronger surface agreement at broader tolerances. It also achieves an average ATE RMSE of 1.56cm, showing stable trajectory alignment, with a mean Chamfer distance of 2.40cm. The strongest reconstructions occur on dominant room-scale surfaces, with future refinement focused on improving fine structures, dense clutter and partially observed regions.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [86]
>>
endobj
